  "result": "JWT `exp` field is **Unix seconds**. `Date.now()` returns **milliseconds**.\n\nYour check probably looks like:\n\n```js\nif (decoded.exp < Date.now()) {\n  throw new Error('Token expired');\n}\n```\n\n`decoded.exp` \u2248 `1745000000` (seconds)\n`Date.now()` \u2248 `1745000000000` (ms)\n\n`exp` always less than `Date.now()` \u2192 condition never true \u2192 all tokens pass.\n\n**Fix:**\n\n```js\nif (decoded.exp < Date.now() / 1000) {\n  throw new Error('Token expired');\n}\n```\n\nOr equivalently:\n\n```js\nif (decoded.exp * 1000 < Date.now()) {\n  throw new Error('Token expired');\n}\n```\n\nBoth correct. First form cleaner. Also consider using `jsonwebtoken`'s built-in verification \u2014 `jwt.verify()` checks expiry automatically, no manual comparison needed.",
